  "docText": [
    "SOLAR®",
    "Biamp Design System",
    "1.0",
    "Text Input",
    "Description",
    "Single-line text field for free-form user input — names, emails, search, identifiers, short answers. Label sits above; helper text below; mandatory asterisk optional. Validate on blur, not per-keystroke.",
    "Sizes",
    "sm (36px)    Dense forms, inspector panes, table inline edits.\nmd (44px)    Default for page-level forms and full-width layouts.",
    "States (⚠ rename pending)",
    "default      resting.\nhover        border lifts to border/feedback/focus/subtle.\nactive       focused, cursor in field. Flagged to rename to `focus` to match SOLAR state vocab.\nfilled        has user content.\ndisabled    opacity/disabled, not-allowed cursor.\nerror         color/border/feedback/danger/strong + error helper text.",
    "Content",
    "Labels: short, sentence case, describe the data (\"Email address\", \"Project name\"). Helper text: 1 line, plain language, set expectation (\"We'll never share it\"). Error: plain language with the fix (\"Enter a valid email address\"), not the complaint (\"Invalid input\"). Mandatory: either consistently mark required OR mark optional — pick one.",
    "Accessibility",
    "Render as <input> with a real <label for=\"\">. Placeholder never substitutes for label (WCAG 3.3.2). Error has aria-describedby pointing at the error text. Mandatory uses aria-required. Focus ring via shadow/focus/default. Contrast: text ≥ 4.5:1 against surface.",
    "Rules",
    "Do\n\n• Label every input with a visible <label>\n• Validate on blur, not on every keystroke\n• Write errors as 'how to fix', not 'what's wrong'\n• Match type attribute to data (email, tel, url)",
    "Don't\n\n• Don't use placeholder text as the label\n• Don't show red errors while the user is still typing\n• Don't mix 'required' and 'optional' markers in the same form\n• Don't put destructive cleanup (clear-on-focus) on a text input"
  ],
